# Repository policy
#
# Committed: build scripts, documentation, research provenance (source snapshots and
# metadata), and the media the build actually consumes (.build/clips/*.mp4 + posters).
# Excluded: the large rendered deliverables, raw download staging, vendored Python/Node
# dependencies, and regenerable render output. See README.md for how to rebuild them.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Rendered deliverables — rebuild with .build/build_selfcontained.py
# The self-contained deck is ~132 MB, above GitHub's 100 MB per-file limit, so each
# built version is published as a GitHub release asset instead of committed.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Agents_for_Robotics_Self_Contained.html
output/Agents_for_Robotics_Focused.pptx
output/Agents_for_Robotics_Offline_Player.zip
output/Agents_for_Robotics_Static_Preview.pdf
.build/standalone_isolation/
.build/draft.pptx
.build/focus_media.pptx
.build/*.pdf

# Offline player bundle (historical 22-slide deliverable). Only media_credits.json is
# kept, because build_selfcontained.py reads it as a build input.
output/offline_player/media/
output/offline_player/posters/
output/offline_player/slides/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Vendored third-party dependencies — reinstall, do not version
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.build/font_deps/
.build/static_render_deps/
.build/qa_deps/
.build/node_modules
node_modules/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Raw download staging. Source URLs and SHA-256 for every file are recorded in
# .build/media_downloads.json, .build/continuation_downloads.json and
# .build/community_downloads.json; .build/clips/ holds the encoded clips the
# build actually embeds and those ARE committed.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.build/assets/*.mp4
.build/assets/*.gif
.build/assets/*.png
.build/assets/*.svg
.build/assets/*.webp
.build/assets/*.partial
.build/previews/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Regenerable renders and scratch state
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.build/rendered/
.build/focus_rendered/*.png
.build/final_artifact_rendered/
.build/final_pdf_rendered/
.build/standalone_rendered/
.build/direct_first_static_rendered/
.build/three_parts_static_rendered/
.build/lo-preview/
.build/final-lo-preview/
.build/lo-profile/
.build/lo-final-profile/
.build/*.log

# Superseded revision backups: the source files are kept, the 110 MB rendered deck
# from each backup is not.
.build/prior_*/**/Agents_for_Robotics_Self_Contained.html

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Not part of this talk
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Rendered pages of a different presentation, kept locally only as a typography
# reference. Nothing in the build reads them.
.build/reference/
.build/reference_review.html

# GitHub code-search results for the query "empire", which collided with the ENPIRE
# paper name and returned unrelated third-party repositories. No research value.
research/searches/github_empire.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OS and editor noise
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Local v0.6 provenance staging and regenerated previews
.build/revision_0_6_baseline/
.build/revision_0_6_screens/
.build/assets/v0_6/*.mp4

# Local v0.7 source/delivery snapshot and regenerated visual checks
.build/revision_0_7_baseline/
.build/revision_0_7_screens/

# Publication cleanup: regenerable screenshots and unpinned download staging.
# Hash-pinned originals used by source-verification gates remain versioned below.
.build/v*_visual/
.build/v*_video_review/
.build/*.png
.build/assets/**/*.mp4
.build/assets/**/*.pdf
